# The build context of ia/Dockerfile (docker build ... ia): the image copies
# only requirements.txt, fespp_ia/ and tests/, so what else this folder holds
# stays out of the context, above all the models (gigabytes each), which the
# service reads from its /models volume and never from the image.
# ia/Dockerfile.model builds from ia/models itself, a context this file does
# not apply to: ia/build-models.ps1 writes that context's own .dockerignore.
# Each folder is named with and without /**, as in the root .dockerignore, so
# that a builder reading the bare name as the folder alone drops its content
# too.
models
models/**
corpus
corpus/**
corpus_cache
corpus_cache/**
**/__pycache__
